From 9fe231b2a5b09d1a6c565ef6383ebc120c49970d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grizbeard <justin.morken@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 15:57:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] Clear the long-press pixmap before painting the button
 into it

The long-press latching animation captures the button's off state into a
QPixmap and wipes it away across the button. A fresh QPixmap holds
undefined bytes, and what paintOnDevice draws onto it does not
necessarily cover all of them: a stylesheet background is drawn
antialiased, so along the button's edge it blends with whatever was
already there. That is uninitialised memory, and the wipe drags a fringe
of random colour across the button for the length of the animation.

Fill it transparent first.

Seen on a skin whose buttons are flat stylesheet fills with no border
image, where the blend at the edge is the only thing that touches those
bytes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/widget/wpushbutton.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/widget/wpushbutton.cpp b/src/widget/wpushbutton.cpp
index 30c8c387..11f48b9a 100644
--- a/src/widget/wpushbutton.cpp
+++ b/src/widget/wpushbutton.cpp
@@ -586,6 +586,12 @@ void WPushButton::LongPressLatching::start() {
             static_cast<int>(
                     m_pButton->height() * m_pButton->devicePixelRatio()));
     m_preLongPressPixmap.setDevicePixelRatio(m_pButton->devicePixelRatio());
+    // A fresh QPixmap holds undefined bytes, and what is painted onto it next
+    // does not necessarily cover all of them: a stylesheet background is drawn
+    // antialiased, so along the button's edge it blends with whatever was
+    // already there. Left unfilled that is uninitialised memory, and the
+    // latching animation drags a fringe of random colour across the button.
+    m_preLongPressPixmap.fill(Qt::transparent);
     m_pButton->paintOnDevice(&m_preLongPressPixmap, 0);
     // ... and start the long press latching animation
     m_sinceStart.start();
